# Skills shipped to the SDK at install time.
# CMake reads this list and copies each named file from skills/ to the SDK
# under <DAS_INSTALL_DOCDIR>/skills/. Single source of truth: top-level skills/.
# Edit this list when adding a user-facing (vs repo-internal) skill.
#
# INVARIANT: if a skill on this list references `skills/<other>.md`, that other
# skill must be on the list too, or the SDK ships a dangling link. The
# aot_testing / llvm_tune / perf_lint / style_lint entries below are here for
# exactly that reason (cross-referenced from cpp_integration, writing_tests,
# daspkg, das_macros, and strings). The invariant cuts both ways: a repo-only
# skill stays off the list and any shipped skill pointing at it gets reworded
# instead -- that is why tutorials.md is absent (it would drag in
# documentation_rst.md, and onward).
#
# Keep this file ASCII-only, comments included: CMake's file(STRINGS) treats
# non-ASCII bytes as separators, so an em-dash inside a comment splits the line
# and the tail gets read as a skill filename.
aot_testing.md
clargs_usage.md
cpp_integration.md
das_formatting.md
das_macros.md
dashv.md
daslang_live.md
daslib_modules.md
daspkg.md
decs.md
detect_dupe.md
dynamic_modules.md
external_module_debugging.md
filesystem.md
find_dupe.md
gc_migration.md
glob.md
imgui_ui_debugging.md
jobque_debugging.md
json.md
linq.md
llvm_tune.md
mcp_tools.md
memory_leak_detection.md
perf_lint.md
project_overview.md
regex.md
sql.md
strings.md
strudel_port.md
style_lint.md
writing_tests.md
xml.md
